Tenda Nova MW5 v43.12 built-in wired diagnostics
================================================

One-command automatic test:

  mw5-netdiag

The automatic test first waits for OpenWrt netifd/LAN to be fully ready. Start
with the Ethernet cable in the physical LAN jack. The script tests normal LAN
through br-lan and its DHCP/peer path, then direct LAN. When prompted, move the
same cable to the physical WAN jack for direct WAN. After the original network
is restored, the script also checks routed WAN DHCP while the cable remains in
WAN.

No additional router or PC commands are required. A PC left on DHCP/automatic
can be discovered and pinged automatically. For the final routed-WAN DHCP
check, connect WAN to an upstream DHCP router if you want a real lease test;
with a direct PC connection, NO-LEASE is expected and is simply recorded.

Firewall policy:

  Standard OpenWrt firewall4 configuration is retained.
  LAN and WAN use the normal OpenWrt zones and forwarding policy.
  The diagnostic script does not flush nftables or disable firewall4.

Manual/read-only modes remain available:

  mw5-netdiag help
  mw5-netdiag state
  mw5-netdiag full
  mw5-netdiag direct auto
  mw5-netdiag direct lan
  mw5-netdiag direct wan
  mw5-netdiag restore

v43.12 hardware focus:

  * switch->CPU RX accepts the observed 0x8899/0x0400+source-port layout
    (0x0401 was captured from physical LAN port 1).
  * CPU->switch TX uses protocol 0x9 plus destination mask only:
    LAN port 1 = 0x9002, WAN port 3 = 0x9008 (no speculative bit 9).
  * RX completion follows OEM USE_SWITCH_RX_CDP and TX reclamation follows
    OEM USE_SWITCH_TX_CDP; CPURPDCR0/CPUTPDCR0 remain authoritative.
  * The MW5 now uses the OEM CRC/FCS length convention: EXCLUDE_CRC is clear,
    RX length has FCS stripped before Linux, and TX descriptor length includes
    the hardware-generated four-byte FCS.
  * Six-dword/24-byte RX/TX descriptors are accessed through the matching
    uncached KSEG1 CPU alias, mirroring the OEM UNCACHE_MASK path.
  * Only TX ring 0 is enabled; ring 1 is no longer left enabled without its
    own CPUTPDCR/length configuration. TX EOR is omitted in tail-aware mode.
  * bounded RX bad-descriptor payload snapshots and TX completion traces are
    collected by the one-command test.

Driver state is readable from /proc/rd05-rtknet.
All reports are written below /tmp/mw5-diag.
The last automatic summary is /tmp/mw5-diag/autotest-summary-latest.txt.
